{
    "background_story": "Tristan was a young monk who lived in a secluded monastery nestled in the rolling hills of medieval Europe. He spent most of his days pouring over ancient texts, seeking to deepen his understanding of the scriptures. Tristan's fascination with the written word led him to become a skilled scribe, meticulously copying sacred texts by hand. His attention to detail and devotion to his craft earned him recognition among the monastic community. As he delved deeper into the scriptures, Tristan began to see parallels between the ancient stories and the world around him. He started to write his own scriptural interpretations, weaving together the threads of faith, history, and everyday life. His writings became a source of inspiration for his fellow monks and eventually spread to the wider community, earning Tristan a reputation as a wise and insightful scholar.",
